WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.280
In October 1973, an oil
embargo hits the United States.

2
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.100
The price of oil jumps
from 2.90 dollars a barrel

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:15.410
to 11.65 dollars by January 1974.

4
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.450
From November 1973, the US
economy is in recession.

5
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.070
Yet prices keep rising fast.

6
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:24.760
Usually, when AD falls,
inflation falls too.

7
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.540
So how can an economy
produce less and charge

8
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.500
more at the same time?

9
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.370
In this mission, you'll
see why firms supply more

10
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.110
when the price level rises,

11
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.750
at least in the short run.

12
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.560
Then you'll use a graph
lab to shock the economy

13
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.590
and track PL and real GDP.

14
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.910
Your mission: explain how
one shock can mean higher

15
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.390
prices and lower output together.
